this is a proposal of a new functionality in testthat - mock objects;
I haven't really made it complete yet and it is meant to serve as an example of what could be done

my goal here is to see whether this is interesting for other developers at all

This adds pending tests

``` R
# unit test syntax
test_that("my test", {
  pending("hasn't been implemented")
})

# bdd syntax
describe("feature", {
  it("can have not yet tested specs") # implicit call to pending()
  it("can have not yet tested specs with partial implementation", {
    # some code
    pending("not yet done")
  })
})
```

This also modifies the summary reporter to display pending tests. I haven't changed other reporters.
I don't know if that the is smartest way to implement this, but it's a start :) I basically added a pending state to the expectation struct. 

What do you think? Does that makes sense for the package?
